<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103949" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίλ-μα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything pulled</i> or <i>shredded, lint</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Decent.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, Heraclid.
				Tarent.
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.957
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>anything that can be pulled</i> or <i>plucked</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.48b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίλσις</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				2.69
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in
			later Medic. language, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίλματα</span>
			<i>sprains</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(1).682
			</span></i>.</div>
